== Notes ==
* Brownie may be paired along with regular {{e|Dip}}s in a Boss Room.
* If a {{i|Butt Bombs}} Bomb goes off in the same room as Brownie, it heals him.
** {{dlc|a+}} Butt Bombs effect on {{i|Dr. Fetus}} or {{i|Epic Fetus}} does not heal Brownie.
** {{dlc|r}} The skeleton version of {{c|Tainted Forgotten}} in the [[Hot Potato]] challenge <u>does</u> heal Brownie. Thus, butt bombs should be skipped to avoid a potential softlock.
* {{i|Flush!}} kills Brownie instantly and causes him to leave behind 6 {{e|Brownie Corn}}s.
* If Brownie is inflicted by any [[status effect]], he leaves a [[creep]] with that same effect (e.g. {{i|Spider Bite}} gives him [[white creep]] if he's affected).

== Trivia ==
* Brownie is the name of a character and boss in [[wikipedia:Super Meat Boy|Super Meat Boy]], a game by Edmund McMillen (the creator of ''The Binding of Isaac'').
* In the versus screen, there is a smiling face next to Brownie's name.
* The Black Champion version of Brownie acts slightly similar to the Dank Squirt and may, therefore, be a "dank" or [[wikipedia:meconium|meconium]] version of Brownie.
* During the DLC's release, the Black Champion version of Brownie was able to spawn up to 11 {{e|Drowned Charger}}s at once instead of regular Chargers, at a higher rate. It was nerfed in an update shortly after since the damage from the large amounts of Drowned Chargers was unavoidable.
* {{dlc+|a+}} Brownie can be found in {{s|The Void}}, even before being unlocked.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} Brownie was given a "voice" in [[Repentance]] which he shares with {{e|Clog}}.{{dlc-}}

